Track 3: "Did the Mantis Clear the Cape?"
- Story & Context: Scene folklore claims that when the herring trawler Havsula lost its rudder off the reef of Nordkapp, the skipper navigated back to shore entirely by ear, steering the ship toward the thumping cadence of a bootleg radio broadcast booming from the beacon's horn. In the lighthouse gallery, the band had chained two orchestral timpani together, mimicking the thunder of migrating insects across warm savannahs while tearing through sunny surf-punk cadences. When harbor officials boarded the battered vessel at dawn, they found the entire crew dancing frantically on fish-slick decks, bellowing "drop the lead-line, we can smell the limes" into the morning fog. The recording circulated on pirate flexi-discs pressed from discarded navigational charts, forever enshrining the rescue as a miraculous dancefloor myth.
